---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Cookie Policy | XFour"
	description="Every cookie and browser storage item used on xfour.co.uk: who sets it, what it is for, and how long it lasts."
	liveChat={false}
>
    <section class="clean-block clean-info dark">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="block-heading">
                <h1 class="text-info">Cookie Policy</h1>
                <p>What this website stores on your device, who puts it there, and how to change your mind.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="clean-block">
        <div class="container">
            <article class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 50rem;">

                <h2 class="h4">The short version</h2>
                <p>This site works without cookies. Nothing that needs your permission is stored until you give it.</p>
                <p>The one thing that needs your permission is our <strong>live chat</strong>. It is run for us by Microsoft, and
                    it stores things in your browser as soon as it loads. So it stays switched off until you choose to allow it.
                    If you do not allow it, the chat bubble does not appear and you can still reach us by phone or email.</p>
                <p>We also count visits, but in a way that stores nothing on your device and does not identify you. That is
                    explained under <a href="#measurement">Measurement that stores nothing</a>.</p>

                <p>
                    <a class="btn btn-primary" role="button" href="/legal/cookies" data-x4-consent-open>Change your cookie choices</a>
                </p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Cookies used on this site</h2>
                <p>We last checked this list against the live site on <strong>11 October 2026</strong>. If you find something in
                    your browser that is not described here, please tell us at
                    <a href="mailto:gdpr@xfour.co.uk">gdpr@xfour.co.uk</a> and we will correct this page.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Always on: strictly necessary</h3>
                <p>These two do not need your permission, because the site cannot be secure or remember your choice without
                    them. They hold no name, no email address and nothing that identifies you to us.</p>
                <div class="x4-cookie-table-wrap">
                    <table class="x4-cookie-table">
                        <caption class="visually-hidden">Strictly necessary cookies</caption>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col">Name</th>
                                <th scope="col">Set by</th>
                                <th scope="col">What it is for</th>
                                <th scope="col">How long it lasts</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>x4_consent</code></td>
                                <td>XFour (this website)</td>
                                <td>Remembers the cookie choice you made, so we do not ask you again on every page. It records
                                    only your answer and the date you gave it.</td>
                                <td>12 months</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>cf_clearance</code></td>
                                <td>Cloudflare, who host and protect this site</td>
                                <td>Records that your browser has passed Cloudflare's security check, so you are not asked
                                    again. You will only see it if Cloudflare decided to check your browser.</td>
                                <td>Up to 1 year</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4">Live chat: only if you allow it</h3>
                <p>These are set by Microsoft, not by us, and they are set on Microsoft's own domains rather than ours. They
                    appear when the chat loads and opens. We cannot delete them for you, because they are not ours — if you
                    change your mind, clear them in your browser settings.</p>
                <div class="x4-cookie-table-wrap">
                    <table class="x4-cookie-table">
                        <caption class="visually-hidden">Live chat cookies and browser storage</caption>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col">Name</th>
                                <th scope="col">Set by</th>
                                <th scope="col">What it is for</th>
                                <th scope="col">How long it lasts</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>MC1</code></td>
                                <td>Microsoft (<code>.microsoft.com</code>)</td>
                                <td>Identifies your browser to the Microsoft service that runs our chat.</td>
                                <td>Up to 1 year</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>MS0</code></td>
                                <td>Microsoft (<code>.microsoft.com</code>)</td>
                                <td>Identifies a single session with the Microsoft service that runs our chat.</td>
                                <td>About 30 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td><code>lcwDesignerDisabled-&hellip;</code>,
                                    <code>customNotification-&hellip;</code>,
                                    <code>customStartChatError-&hellip;</code></td>
                                <td>Microsoft, in the chat widget's own storage</td>
                                <td>Browser storage, not cookies. Holds how the chat window should look and behave, and the
                                    wording of its messages, so it does not have to fetch them again.</td>
                                <td>About 24 hours</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>One item with a 32&#8209;character name</td>
                                <td>Microsoft, in the chat widget's own storage</td>
                                <td>Browser storage, not a cookie. Internal state for the chat widget. Microsoft does not
                                    document what it holds, and we cannot read it.</td>
                                <td>Until you clear your browser storage</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>If you start a conversation, what you type is also sent to our Dynamics 365 system so that we can answer
                    you. That is covered in our <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5" id="measurement">Measurement that stores nothing</h2>
                <p>Two tools count visits to this site. Neither sets a cookie and neither writes anything to your device, so
                    neither one needs your permission under the cookie rules. We list them anyway, because you should be able
                    to find out who sees your visit.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>PostHog</strong>, hosted in the European Union, counts page views and clicks on our phone,
                        email and booking links. It is set to its cookieless mode: instead of storing an identifier on your
                        device, the server works one out from the day, your network address and your browser type. That value
                        is rebuilt every day, so it cannot be used to follow you from one day to the next. Session recording
                        and surveys are switched off.</li>
                    <li><strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> reports how quickly pages loaded and which pages were
                        visited. Cloudflare adds it at their end, so it is not in our website code. It uses no cookies.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>If you press <strong>Reject</strong> on our cookie banner, or turn off visit measurement in your cookie
                    choices, we stop PostHog from collecting anything about you. Cloudflare Web Analytics is added by our
                    hosting rather than by our pages, so we cannot switch it off per visitor; your browser's
                    <em>Do Not Track</em> setting is honoured by PostHog.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Other companies your browser contacts</h2>
                <p>Some of the fonts, icons and code libraries this site uses are served by other companies. Your browser has
                    to ask them for those files, so they can see your network address and which page you were on. They do not
                    set cookies on our pages. They are:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Cloudflare — hosting, security and the font and code libraries served from
                        <code>cdnjs.cloudflare.com</code></li>
                    <li>Google — the Montserrat web font (<code>fonts.googleapis.com</code>)</li>
                    <li>Fonticons — the Font Awesome icons (<code>use.fontawesome.com</code>)</li>
                    <li>jsDelivr — the Bootstrap code library (<code>cdn.jsdelivr.net</code>)</li>
                    <li>Microsoft — the live chat, but only once you have allowed it</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">How to change your mind</h2>
                <p>Use the <strong>Cookie choices</strong> link in the footer of any page, or the button near the top of this
                    page. Your choice is remembered for 12 months, after which we will ask again.</p>
                <p>Turning the live chat off stops it loading the next time a page opens. It cannot remove cookies Microsoft
                    has already set — to do that, clear cookies in your browser settings. Every major browser also lets you
                    block or delete cookies for a whole site; if you block ours, the site still works, but we will have to ask
                    you about cookies again on every page.</p>

                <h2 class="h4 mt-5">Questions</h2>
                <p>Email <a href="mailto:gdpr@xfour.co.uk">gdpr@xfour.co.uk</a>. The data controller is XFour IT Limited,
                    company number 11776254, registered office 100 Berkshire Place, C/O KT Wells Ltd, Winnersh Triangle,
                    Wokingham, RG41 5RD.</p>
                <p>See also our <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>, which explains what we do with personal
                    information, and our <a href="/legal/legal">legal and company information</a>.</p>

                <p class="text-muted mt-5"><small>Last updated 11 October 2026.</small></p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
